      "description": "What an AUTHOR creates using the graph -- a note, a visualization, a paper -- referencing the KG and rendered through the harness's just-the-docs document rendering. It declares the EXISTING `folio` kind rather than a new one: `folio` is 'authored content, rendered to a website', registered by core because only core can render it. The contrast is with `docs` in cat-harness, whose subject is the harness itself. Example: a catalogue goes in `library/` or is referenced remotely; a note ABOUT it is a folio; the page explaining how ingestion works is docs.",
